id: pm-rl-upe0
title: Bounded LM trainer adapter for the recursive loop
description: "Implement the bounded causal-LM trainer adapter for pm rl loop run: a tiny decoder-only transformer in TypeScript (1 layer, single-head causal attention, d_model<=48, Float32Array, hand-written forward/backward with a finite-difference gradient-check test over every parameter tensor), a deterministically regenerated frozen base policy pretrained on a synthetic copy task, LoRA-style low-rank adapters (rank<=4) on Q/V and the output head trained by REINFORCE with mean baseline, KL penalty to the base policy and gradient clipping, content-addressed adapter checkpoints with canonical serialization, declared fail-closed limits (max parameters, checkpoint bytes, steps, wall seconds, licences), and held-out exact-match evaluation through the existing Hoeffding promotion gate. Reuses loop.ts machinery: one gate, one promotion path."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: execution,llm-adapter,recursive-training
created_at: "2026-10-06T12:49:29.811Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-06T15:14:16.805Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: "A real pm CLI acceptance run of >=3 generations where gen-1 and gen-2 checkpoints differ, gen-2 collects with gen-1's promoted adapter asserted via receipts, held-out exact-match strictly improves over the base, and a contaminated run is refused; unit, property (gradient check, seed determinism), integration and performance budget tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; docs/lm-adapter.md records the measured generation table"
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-06T12:49:36.273Z",pi-glm,"Starting the bounded LM trainer adapter slice in the package worktree on branch feat/lm-policy-adapter. Plan: (1) prototype the tiny transformer + REINFORCE offline to pick sizes that keep the acceptance run under ~20s on CPU, (2) author lm.ts mirroring systemone.ts contracts (parse/execute/verify/promotion scores/seed configs), (3) wire the lm trainer into loop.ts/index.ts dispatch without forking the controller, (4) tests: unit+property (finite-difference gradient check over every parameter tensor, seed determinism), integration + CLI acceptance + performance budget, (5) docs/lm-adapter.md + README + RECURSIVE_TRAINING status."
  "2026-10-06T14:36:39.057Z",codex-sol,"Continuing the existing bounded LM feature: audit inherited math, trainer lineage and receipts; verify focused tests; commit logical progress early; then complete CLI evidence, full release gates and documentation."
  "2026-10-06T14:38:31.079Z",codex-sol,"Inherited draft verification: npm ci and npm run typecheck passed; node --test test/lm.test.ts test/lm-loop.test.ts passed 20/20, including finite differences over every base and adapter tensor. The existing acceptance uses the SDK command harness, so a spawned real CLI acceptance and manual measured run are still required. Audit found missing filesystem checkpoint artifacts, differing hash/serialization payloads, squared L2 reporting, and incomplete resource enforcement; retaining this passing draft as an early progress checkpoint before corrections."
  "2026-10-06T14:51:13.556Z",codex-sol,"Corrected the draft to sequence-reward REINFORCE with the batch mean baseline. Copy pretraining is restricted to declared training content. Checkpoint digests now hash the exact canonical stored bytes; immutable artifacts are persisted and checked before replay advances. Parameters include the frozen base, optimizer limits reserve pretraining plus every declared generation, and clock guards stop CPU work between batches and sampled episodes. Focused suite passed 20/20 after fixture correction; the first packed real CLI proof ran three generations in 9.03s with two promotions and a third-generation regression refusal. Full source coverage remains in progress."
  "2026-10-06T14:57:31.971Z",codex-sol,"Manual packed real CLI CPU run: Node v24.19.0; command pm rl loop run manual --file cfg.json --approval approval --json in a scratch pm project; command wall 17793.628 ms; 2912 total parameters (2560 frozen, 352 trainable); base greedy exact-match 0; 192 collection samples; two promotions followed by a regression refusal. Generation table:\n1: source=sha256:058aa3d2c08438abd18cf0e9b455aca99ddb95492de852201c55c79a0672130d; candidate=sha256:37e503748a170be32e1d506997b6c0cc5c9ee256b24ab01fb49cf0564da07b4c; greedy_exact_match=0.0625; held_out_reward=0.183854; promoted=true; delta_l2=2.682299; checkpoint_bytes=7705\n2: source=sha256:37e503748a170be32e1d506997b6c0cc5c9ee256b24ab01fb49cf0564da07b4c; candidate=sha256:086f78992283cba37929321abe3961ca6132a52c332bf8a8387a52f22141cbdb; greedy_exact_match=0.0625; held_out_reward=0.292396; promoted=true; delta_l2=2.831507; checkpoint_bytes=7621\n3: source=sha256:086f78992283cba37929321abe3961ca6132a52c332bf8a8387a52f22141cbdb; candidate=sha256:2a6f8b9dac4232c6b4576c315d298f530be5705e0e148fd5fbf3b9c282a9f02e; greedy_exact_match=0.0625; held_out_reward=0.227292; promoted=false; delta_l2=2.491317; checkpoint_bytes=7596\nGeneration 2 collection component and receipt source equal generation 1 promoted digest. Final policy stays at generation 2. Renamed held-out training content is refused with lm_dataset_overlap. Full digests, phase times and resource contract are in docs/lm-adapter.md."
  "2026-10-06T15:01:31.142Z",codex-sol,"Focused instrumented numerical/durable tests pass with lm.ts at 100% lines, branches and functions. Native Bun command bun test --timeout 120000 test/lm.test.ts test/lm-loop.test.ts test/lm-cli.test.ts passed 29/29; its packed real CLI command took 6.307s and reproduced the Node digests and scores. pm test pm-rl-upe0 --run --progress passed both linked commands (typecheck and 15 LM unit/property tests); test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment records the result. Full npm and Bun release gates are still pending. The repo changelog:full script was regenerated after tracker writes; open features are excluded by its closed-only default, so the generated changelog is unchanged while this item remains open."
  "2026-10-06T15:14:03.769Z",codex-sol,"The broad release suite passed 430/430 tests but coverage correctly refused at 99.99% lines / 99.97% branches: one guard for an existing candidate with missing collection evidence was not exercised. Added the real lost-evidence replay drill (passing), and inlined the single-use RNG wrapper to meet the no-trivial-one-call-helper rule without changing draws. Re-running both full release gates against the committed source; no thresholds or source inventory entries are weakened."
  "2026-10-06T15:14:16.805Z",codex-sol,"Correction to the preceding broad-suite count: the runner reported 427/427 passing tests, not 430. The only uncovered source was index.ts lines 3100-3101 (the stored-candidate missing-collection guard); lm.ts itself was 100% lines, branches and functions."
